@@ -89,7 +89,7 @@ cmake -B build-web -S azahar -G Ninja -DCMAKE_BUILD_TYPE=Release -DBUILD_SHARED_
 cmake --build build-web --parallel 8
 ```
 
-The generated `azahar.html`, `azahar.js`, and `azahar.wasm` files are placed in `build-web/bin/Release/`; copy the JS and WASM files beside `web/index.html`. This build uses Emscripten pthreads (a 32-worker pool), so it must be served with `Cross-Origin-Opener-Policy: same-origin` and `Cross-Origin-Embedder-Policy: require-corp` headers. The supplied server also sends a same-origin resource policy header. From the workspace root, use it with:
+The generated `azahar.html`, `azahar.js`, and `azahar.wasm` files are placed in `build-web/bin/Release/`. A normal CMake build automatically synchronizes the JS and WASM files beside `web/index.html`; `build_web.bat` also verifies their hashes. This build uses Emscripten pthreads (a 32-worker pool), so it must be served with `Cross-Origin-Opener-Policy: same-origin` and `Cross-Origin-Embedder-Policy: require-corp` headers. The supplied server also sends a same-origin resource policy header. From the workspace root, use it with:
 
 ```powershell
 node web/server.cjs
@@ -97,6 +97,8 @@ node web/server.cjs
 
 Then open `http://127.0.0.1:8765/`. The web target starts with 512MB of shared memory, may grow to 4GB, and uses a 2MB stack setting.
 
+For LAN testing on port 9000, run `serve_web.bat` and open `http://<your-LAN-IP>:9000/web/index.html` (the supplied server accepts both `/` and `/web/index.html`). Do not use a generic static server unless it sends the same COOP/COEP headers. On static HTTPS hosting such as GitHub Pages, the bundled `coi-serviceworker.js` adds those headers after one controlled reload; plain HTTP LAN IPs still require a header-aware server.
+
 The browser path has been verified with a legally owned, decrypted `.3ds` kiosk demo image: it reaches a visible Super Mario 3D Land title framebuffer in the browser after its boot period. Encrypted CIA files are intentionally rejected with a clear error; extract and use a decrypted cartridge image, keeping its `.3ds` extension. This software-rendered interpreter path is still substantially below full 3DS speed, so browser execution remains experimental and is not a general compatibility guarantee.
 
